Client : Product based company Role : Peppol Compliance / Tax SME Shift Timings: APAC Shift(6 AM to 3 PM/6:30 AM to 3:30 PM) Location: Remote Experience : 5+ Years Work Mode: Hybrid Interview Mode: Virtual Interview Mode of hire Permanent with OTSi Job Description: We are seeking an experienced Compliance / Tax Subject Matter Expert (SME) to support a multi-market Peppol e-invoicing compliance and finance transformation program across APAC.
produce a compliance gap report Advise on country-specific business rules (e.g., Peppol BIS/PINT SG, MyInvois XML/PINT MY, PINT A-NZ, JP PINT) and how they affect invoice data fields, validation rules and archival requirements Partner with the Business Analyst and Solution Architect to ensure the future-state process design and technical architecture satisfy all applicable compliance and audit-trail requirements Contribute to the prioritized, market-by-market compliance roadmap and participate in design walkthroughs and sign-off Flag jurisdiction-specific risks (tender eligibility, penalty exposure, data-residency or retention rules) early enough to influence design decisions Validate that test scenarios and conformance/certification testing correctly reflect regulatory business rules Respond to compliance questions arising during build, integration and UAT Review exception-handling and validation logic for tax and regulatory accuracy before go-live Monitor for regulatory changes or mandate timeline shifts in active markets and flag any design impact Support go-live readiness and hypercare on compliance-related issues Contribute to the governance and continuous-compliance framework for post-go-live sustainment Required Qualifications & Experience 5+ years of experience in indirect tax, e-invoicing compliance, tax technology, or regulatory advisory, ideally within a Big 4, tax consultancy, or in-house tax/compliance function Direct working knowledge of Peppol (4-corner/5-corner model, UBL/PINT standards) and at least one APAC e-invoicing mandate (Singapore InvoiceNow, Malaysia MyInvois, Australia/NZ Peppol, or Japan's Qualified Invoice System) Strong understanding of AP and AR processes and how tax/compliance rules intersect with invoice data, validation and archival Experience translating regulatory requirements into practical business and system requirements for a delivery team (not purely advisory comfortable working inside a project/delivery context) Familiarity with multi-entity, multi-jurisdiction corporate structures and the compliance complexity they introduce Strong stakeholder communication skills;
able to explain regulatory nuance clearly to both technical teams and executive stakeholders Preferred / Nice to Have Prior experience on a live Peppol or e-invoicing implementation project (client-side or consulting-side) Exposure to multiple APAC markets simultaneously (not just domestic tax experience) Familiarity with ERP-side AP/AR modules (SAP, Oracle, NetSuite, Microsoft Dynamics) and how tax configuration is typically implemented Relevant professional qualification (e.g., CTA, CPA with tax specialization, or equivalent regional tax credential) Key Deliverables Compliance gap assessment report Market-by-market regulatory obligation map and prioritized roadmap Compliance input to future-state process design and control matrix Validated test scenarios and certification sign-off support Ongoing mandate-change monitoring notes / compliance risk flags Thanks, Kishor Pasham [email removed]

